    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0411" n="295" xml:id="pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.E/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-01T13:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1923—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. I am informed by the Brazilian Ambassador that as a result of pressure
                    brought by the President of Chile, he has received instructions to endeavor to
                    persuade the Government of Mexico to reconsider its action in declining the
                    invitation to take part in the Fifth Pan American Conference at Santiago. He
                    said that he had not yet received a reply from the Mexican Government, and
                    intimated that one had not been made because the authorities feared that the
                    delegates from the United States might place the Mexican delegates in an
                    embarrassing position by making reservations to agreements or conventions. I
                    await instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
